** 6. Learning Outcomes:-

- Learned to formulate a maze as a state space problem (state, actions, goal test, cost).
- Implemented uninformed (BFS, DFS) and heuristic (Hill Climbing, Best First, A*) searches.
- Understood the role of a heuristic such as Manhattan distance.
- Saw why Hill Climbing can fail at a local optimum, while A* stays optimal.
- Compared algorithms using path length, nodes explored and execution time.

